Sources of the data files in this folder
========================================

trees.json, patterns.json, constraint_types.json
-------------------------------------------------

Built by ../rulebook.py from the I-ADOPT Patterns,
https://github.com/mabablue/I-ADOPT-patterns-playground
at commit ecca3470bebc90cc70ce6dca9785f2dd3bf7f9c0 (2026-11-09).

The I-ADOPT Patterns were modelled by Barbara Magagna, Sirko Schindler, Stuart Chalk and
Marvin Friedl. They are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ ; see the LICENSE file of
that repository.

Changes made here:

- The decision trees (Mermaid flowcharts), the pattern files and the table of constraint types
  were read into JSON. The files of one numbered pattern were merged into one entry with its
  name, definition, design note and the shapes it asks for.
- The patterns' "example" and "gh_issue" fields were left out.
- Pattern 44 (reference area) is filed as a matrix pattern, as the trees and the example tags
  use it.
- One tree leaf was corrected: DT3 node F now ends on pattern 114. The reason is stored under
  "corrections" in trees.json.
- One answer label was shortened: in DT5, "false:VolumicDensity" became "false".
- The four slips found in the upstream trees while reading them are listed under "slips" in
  trees.json.

issues_snapshot.json, route_key.json
------------------------------------

Built by ../route_key.py from the issues of the I-ADOPT examples repository,
https://github.com/mabablue/I-ADOPT-examples-playground
as they were on 2026-11-19: issue number, title, state, date of last update, labels and the
corpus file each issue links to. route_key.json holds the same labels read as pattern tags for
the 102 corpus variables.

That repository declares no licence.

Not in this folder
------------------

The variable definitions and gold decompositions come from the I-ADOPT corpus,
https://github.com/i-adopt/Corpus, tag v2.0.1, as the lab loads it.
